    "beyond": "lobby",
    "open": 1,
    "openTo": 0
   },
   "text": "My name is Ana. I'm a night nurse. Twelve hour shifts, home at three A.M. Every night, the same routine.",
   "pause": 0.25
  },
  {
   "scene": "street",
   "p": {
    "lit": 1,
    "zoom": 0.15,
    "pops": [
     {
      "at": 1.0,
      "type": "date",
      "text": "BUILT 1961",
      "x": 0.5,
      "y": 0.15
     }
    ]
   },
   "text": "The Harrow Street apartments were built in 1961. Twelve floors, red brick, one old elevator with a brass door that still sticks in winter.",
   "pause": 0.25
  },
  {
   "scene": "elevator",
   "p": {
    "floor": "1",
    "lead": true,
    "eyes": "closed"
   },
   "text": "I've taken that elevator maybe two thousand times. I could ride it with my eyes closed. Some nights, after a double shift, I basically do.",
   "pause": 0.25
  },
  {
   "scene": "lobby",
   "p": {
    "manager": true
   },
   "text": "Wave at Mister Haskell at the front desk. He's run this building for forty years. He never seems to sleep either.",
   "pause": 0.25
  },
  {
